#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-interpret-trailers(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:7
msgid ""
"git-interpret-trailers - Add or parse structured information in commit "
"messages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'git interpret-trailers' [--in-place] [--trim-empty]\n"
"\t\t\t[(--trailer (<key>|<key-alias>)[(=|:)<value>])...]\n"
"\t\t\t[--parse] [<file>...]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:20
msgid ""
"Add or parse 'trailer' lines that look similar to RFC 822 e-mail headers, at "
"the end of the otherwise free-form part of a commit message. For example, in "
"the following commit message"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:23
#, no-wrap
msgid "subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:28
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:345
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Signed-off-by: Alice <alice@example.com>\n"
"Signed-off-by: Bob <bob@example.com>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:31
msgid "the last two lines starting with \"Signed-off-by\" are trailers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:37
msgid ""
"This command reads commit messages from either the <file> arguments or the "
"standard input if no <file> is specified.  If `--parse` is specified, the "
"output consists of the parsed trailers coming from the input, without "
"influencing them with any command line options or configuration variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:43
msgid ""
"Otherwise, this command applies `trailer.*` configuration variables (which "
"could potentially add new trailers, as well as reposition them), as well as "
"any command line arguments that can override configuration variables (such "
"as `--trailer=...` which could also add new trailers), to each input "
"file. The result is emitted on the standard output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:50
msgid ""
"This command can also operate on the output of linkgit:git-format-patch[1], "
"which is more elaborate than a plain commit message. Namely, such output "
"includes a commit message (as above), a \"---\" divider line, and a patch "
"part.  For these inputs, the divider and patch parts are not modified by "
"this command and are emitted as is on the output, unless `--no-divider` is "
"specified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:55
msgid ""
"Some configuration variables control the way the `--trailer` arguments are "
"applied to each input and the way any existing trailer in the input is "
"changed. They also make it possible to automatically add some trailers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:62
msgid ""
"By default, a '<key>=<value>' or '<key>:<value>' argument given using "
"`--trailer` will be appended after the existing trailers only if the last "
"trailer has a different (<key>, <value>) pair (or if there is no existing "
"trailer). The <key> and <value> parts will be trimmed to remove starting and "
"trailing whitespace, and the resulting trimmed <key> and <value> will appear "
"in the output like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:65
#, no-wrap
msgid "key: value\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:69
msgid ""
"This means that the trimmed <key> and <value> will be separated by `': '` "
"(one colon followed by one space)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:75
msgid ""
"For convenience, a <key-alias> can be configured to make using `--trailer` "
"shorter to type on the command line. This can be configured using the "
"'trailer.<key-alias>.key' configuration variable. The <keyAlias> must be a "
"prefix of the full <key> string, although case sensitivity does not "
"matter. For example, if you have"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:78
#, no-wrap
msgid "trailer.sign.key \"Signed-off-by: \"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:82
msgid ""
"in your configuration, you only need to specify `--trailer=\"sign: foo\"` on "
"the command line instead of `--trailer=\"Signed-off-by: foo\"`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:87
msgid ""
"By default the new trailer will appear at the end of all the existing "
"trailers. If there is no existing trailer, the new trailer will appear at "
"the end of the input. A blank line will be added before the new trailer if "
"there isn't one already."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:96
msgid ""
"Existing trailers are extracted from the input by looking for a group of one "
"or more lines that (i) is all trailers, or (ii) contains at least one "
"Git-generated or user-configured trailer and consists of at least 25% "
"trailers.  The group must be preceded by one or more empty (or "
"whitespace-only) lines.  The group must either be at the end of the input or "
"be the last non-whitespace lines before a line that starts with '---' "
"(followed by a space or the end of the line)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:103
msgid ""
"When reading trailers, there can be no whitespace before or inside the "
"<key>, but any number of regular space and tab characters are allowed "
"between the <key> and the separator. There can be whitespaces before, inside "
"or after the <value>. The <value> may be split over multiple lines with each "
"subsequent line starting with at least one whitespace, like the \"folding\" "
"in RFC 822. Example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:107
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"key: This is a very long value, with spaces and\n"
"  newlines in it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:111
msgid ""
"Note that trailers do not follow (nor are they intended to follow) many of "
"the rules for RFC 822 headers. For example they do not follow the encoding "
"rule."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:114
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--in-place`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:116
msgid "Edit the files in place."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:117
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--trim-empty`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:121
msgid ""
"If the <value> part of any trailer contains only whitespace, the whole "
"trailer will be removed from the output.  This applies to existing trailers "
"as well as new trailers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--trailer <key>[(=|:)<value>]`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:126
msgid ""
"Specify a (<key>, <value>) pair that should be applied as a trailer to the "
"inputs. See the description of this command."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:127
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--where <placement>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:128
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-where`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:137
msgid ""
"Specify where all new trailers will be added.  A setting provided with "
"'--where' overrides the `trailer.where` and any applicable "
"`trailer.<keyAlias>.where` configuration variables and applies to all "
"'--trailer' options until the next occurrence of '--where' or "
"'--no-where'. Upon encountering '--no-where', clear the effect of any "
"previous use of '--where', such that the relevant configuration variables "
"are no longer overridden. Possible placements are `after`, `before`, `end` "
"or `start`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:138
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--if-exists <action>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:139
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-if-exists`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:149
msgid ""
"Specify what action will be performed when there is already at least one "
"trailer with the same <key> in the input.  A setting provided with "
"'--if-exists' overrides the `trailer.ifExists` and any applicable "
"`trailer.<keyAlias>.ifExists` configuration variables and applies to all "
"'--trailer' options until the next occurrence of '--if-exists' or "
"'--no-if-exists'. Upon encountering '--no-if-exists, clear the effect of any "
"previous use of '--if-exists, such that the relevant configuration variables "
"are no longer overridden. Possible actions are `addIfDifferent`, "
"`addIfDifferentNeighbor`, `add`, `replace` and `doNothing`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:150
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--if-missing <action>`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:151
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-if-missing`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:161
msgid ""
"Specify what action will be performed when there is no other trailer with "
"the same <key> in the input.  A setting provided with '--if-missing' "
"overrides the `trailer.ifMissing` and any applicable "
"`trailer.<keyAlias>.ifMissing` configuration variables and applies to all "
"'--trailer' options until the next occurrence of '--if-missing' or "
"'--no-if-missing'. Upon encountering '--no-if-missing, clear the effect of "
"any previous use of '--if-missing, such that the relevant configuration "
"variables are no longer overridden. Possible actions are `doNothing` or "
"`add`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:162
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--only-trailers`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:164
msgid "Output only the trailers, not any other parts of the input."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:165
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--only-input`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:169
msgid ""
"Output only trailers that exist in the input; do not add any from the "
"command-line or by applying `trailer.*` configuration variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:170
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--unfold`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:173
msgid ""
"If a trailer has a value that runs over multiple lines (aka \"folded\"), "
"reformat the value into a single line."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:174
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--parse`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:180
msgid ""
"A convenience alias for `--only-trailers --only-input --unfold`. This makes "
"it easier to only see the trailers coming from the input without influencing "
"them with any command line options or configuration variables, while also "
"making the output machine-friendly with --unfold."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:181
#, no-wrap
msgid "`--no-divider`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:185
msgid ""
"Do not treat `---` as the end of the commit message. Use this when you know "
"your input contains just the commit message itself (and not an email or the "
"output of `git format-patch`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:187
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONFIGURATION VARIABLES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:189
#, no-wrap
msgid "trailer.separators"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:194
msgid ""
"This option tells which characters are recognized as trailer separators. By "
"default only ':' is recognized as a trailer separator, except that '=' is "
"always accepted on the command line for compatibility with other git "
"commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:198
msgid ""
"The first character given by this option will be the default character used "
"when another separator is not specified in the config for this trailer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:205
msgid ""
"For example, if the value for this option is \"%=$\", then only lines using "
"the format '<key><sep><value>' with <sep> containing '%', '=' or '$' and "
"then spaces will be considered trailers. And '%' will be the default "
"separator used, so by default trailers will appear like: '<key>% <value>' "
"(one percent sign and one space will appear between the key and the value)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:206
#, no-wrap
msgid "trailer.where"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:208
msgid "This option tells where a new trailer will be added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:210
msgid "This can be `end`, which is the default, `start`, `after` or `before`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:213
msgid ""
"If it is `end`, then each new trailer will appear at the end of the existing "
"trailers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:216
msgid ""
"If it is `start`, then each new trailer will appear at the start, instead of "
"the end, of the existing trailers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:219
msgid ""
"If it is `after`, then each new trailer will appear just after the last "
"trailer with the same <key>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:222
msgid ""
"If it is `before`, then each new trailer will appear just before the first "
"trailer with the same <key>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:223
#, no-wrap
msgid "trailer.ifexists"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:227
msgid ""
"This option makes it possible to choose what action will be performed when "
"there is already at least one trailer with the same <key> in the input."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:230
msgid ""
"The valid values for this option are: `addIfDifferentNeighbor` (this is the "
"default), `addIfDifferent`, `add`, `replace` or `doNothing`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:234
msgid ""
"With `addIfDifferentNeighbor`, a new trailer will be added only if no "
"trailer with the same (<key>, <value>) pair is above or below the line where "
"the new trailer will be added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:237
msgid ""
"With `addIfDifferent`, a new trailer will be added only if no trailer with "
"the same (<key>, <value>) pair is already in the input."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:240
msgid ""
"With `add`, a new trailer will be added, even if some trailers with the same "
"(<key>, <value>) pair are already in the input."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:245
msgid ""
"With `replace`, an existing trailer with the same <key> will be deleted and "
"the new trailer will be added. The deleted trailer will be the closest one "
"(with the same <key>) to the place where the new one will be added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:248
msgid ""
"With `doNothing`, nothing will be done; that is no new trailer will be added "
"if there is already one with the same <key> in the input."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:249
#, no-wrap
msgid "trailer.ifmissing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:253
msgid ""
"This option makes it possible to choose what action will be performed when "
"there is not yet any trailer with the same <key> in the input."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:256
msgid ""
"The valid values for this option are: `add` (this is the default) and "
"`doNothing`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:258
msgid "With `add`, a new trailer will be added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:260
msgid "With `doNothing`, nothing will be done."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:261
#, no-wrap
msgid "trailer.<keyAlias>.key"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:268
msgid ""
"Defines a <keyAlias> for the <key>. The <keyAlias> must be a prefix (case "
"does not matter) of the <key>. For example, in `git config trailer.ack.key "
"\"Acked-by\"` the \"Acked-by\" is the <key> and the \"ack\" is the "
"<keyAlias>. This configuration allows the shorter `--trailer \"ack:...\"` "
"invocation on the command line using the \"ack\" <keyAlias> instead of the "
"longer `--trailer \"Acked-by:...\"`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:273
msgid ""
"At the end of the <key>, a separator can appear and then some space "
"characters. By default the only valid separator is ':', but this can be "
"changed using the `trailer.separators` config variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:276
msgid ""
"If there is a separator in the key, then it overrides the default separator "
"when adding the trailer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:277
#, no-wrap
msgid "trailer.<keyAlias>.where"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:281
msgid ""
"This option takes the same values as the 'trailer.where' configuration "
"variable and it overrides what is specified by that option for trailers with "
"the specified <keyAlias>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:282
#, no-wrap
msgid "trailer.<keyAlias>.ifexists"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:286
msgid ""
"This option takes the same values as the 'trailer.ifexists' configuration "
"variable and it overrides what is specified by that option for trailers with "
"the specified <keyAlias>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:287
#, no-wrap
msgid "trailer.<keyAlias>.ifmissing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:291
msgid ""
"This option takes the same values as the 'trailer.ifmissing' configuration "
"variable and it overrides what is specified by that option for trailers with "
"the specified <keyAlias>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:292
#, no-wrap
msgid "trailer.<keyAlias>.command"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:298
msgid ""
"Deprecated in favor of 'trailer.<keyAlias>.cmd'.  This option behaves in the "
"same way as 'trailer.<keyAlias>.cmd', except that it doesn't pass anything "
"as argument to the specified command.  Instead the first occurrence of "
"substring $ARG is replaced by the <value> that would be passed as argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:301
msgid ""
"Note that $ARG in the user's command is only replaced once and that the "
"original way of replacing $ARG is not safe."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:305
msgid ""
"When both 'trailer.<keyAlias>.cmd' and 'trailer.<keyAlias>.command' are "
"given for the same <keyAlias>, 'trailer.<keyAlias>.cmd' is used and "
"'trailer.<keyAlias>.command' is ignored."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:306
#, no-wrap
msgid "trailer.<keyAlias>.cmd"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:311
msgid ""
"This option can be used to specify a shell command that will be called once "
"to automatically add a trailer with the specified <keyAlias>, and then "
"called each time a '--trailer <keyAlias>=<value>' argument is specified to "
"modify the <value> of the trailer that this option would produce."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:318
msgid ""
"When the specified command is first called to add a trailer with the "
"specified <keyAlias>, the behavior is as if a special '--trailer "
"<keyAlias>=<value>' argument was added at the beginning of the \"git "
"interpret-trailers\" command, where <value> is taken to be the standard "
"output of the command with any leading and trailing whitespace trimmed off."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:325
msgid ""
"If some '--trailer <keyAlias>=<value>' arguments are also passed on the "
"command line, the command is called again once for each of these arguments "
"with the same <keyAlias>. And the <value> part of these arguments, if any, "
"will be passed to the command as its first argument. This way the command "
"can produce a <value> computed from the <value> passed in the '--trailer "
"<keyAlias>=<value>' argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:327
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:331
msgid ""
"Configure a 'sign' trailer with a 'Signed-off-by' key, and then add two of "
"these trailers to a commit message file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:336
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git config trailer.sign.key \"Signed-off-by\"\n"
"$ cat msg.txt\n"
"subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:340
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"body text\n"
"$ git interpret-trailers --trailer 'sign: Alice <alice@example.com>' "
"--trailer 'sign: Bob <bob@example.com>' <msg.txt\n"
"subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:342
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:354
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:361
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:392
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:398
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:404
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:439
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:463
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:475
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:488
#, no-wrap
msgid "body text\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:348
msgid "Use the `--in-place` option to edit a commit message file in place:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:352
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:473
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ cat msg.txt\n"
"subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:359
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Signed-off-by: Bob <bob@example.com>\n"
"$ git interpret-trailers --trailer 'Acked-by: Alice <alice@example.com>' "
"--in-place msg.txt\n"
"$ cat msg.txt\n"
"subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:364
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Signed-off-by: Bob <bob@example.com>\n"
"Acked-by: Alice <alice@example.com>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:368
msgid ""
"Extract the last commit as a patch, and add a 'Cc' and a 'Reviewed-by' "
"trailer to it:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:373
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git format-patch -1\n"
"0001-foo.patch\n"
"$ git interpret-trailers --trailer 'Cc: Alice <alice@example.com>' --trailer "
"'Reviewed-by: Bob <bob@example.com>' 0001-foo.patch >0001-bar.patch\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:378
msgid ""
"Configure a 'sign' trailer with a command to automatically add a "
"'Signed-off-by: ' with the author information only if there is no "
"'Signed-off-by: ' already, and show how it works:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:382
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ cat msg1.txt\n"
"subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:390
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"body text\n"
"$ git config trailer.sign.key \"Signed-off-by: \"\n"
"$ git config trailer.sign.ifmissing add\n"
"$ git config trailer.sign.ifexists doNothing\n"
"$ git config trailer.sign.cmd 'echo \"$(git config user.name) <$(git config "
"user.email)>\"'\n"
"$ git interpret-trailers --trailer sign <msg1.txt\n"
"subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:396
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Signed-off-by: Bob <bob@example.com>\n"
"$ cat msg2.txt\n"
"subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:402
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Signed-off-by: Alice <alice@example.com>\n"
"$ git interpret-trailers --trailer sign <msg2.txt\n"
"subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:406
#, no-wrap
msgid "Signed-off-by: Alice <alice@example.com>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:410
msgid ""
"Configure a 'fix' trailer with a key that contains a '#' and no space after "
"this character, and show how it works:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:416
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git config trailer.separators \":#\"\n"
"$ git config trailer.fix.key \"Fix #\"\n"
"$ echo \"subject\" | git interpret-trailers --trailer fix=42\n"
"subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:418
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fix #42\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:423
msgid ""
"Configure a 'help' trailer with a cmd use a script `glog-find-author` which "
"search specified author identity from git log in git repository and show how "
"it works:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:430
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ cat ~/bin/glog-find-author\n"
"#!/bin/sh\n"
"test -n \"$1\" && git log --author=\"$1\" --pretty=\"%an <%ae>\" -1 || "
"true\n"
"$ cat msg.txt\n"
"subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:437
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"body text\n"
"$ git config trailer.help.key \"Helped-by: \"\n"
"$ git config trailer.help.ifExists \"addIfDifferentNeighbor\"\n"
"$ git config trailer.help.cmd \"~/bin/glog-find-author\"\n"
"$ git interpret-trailers --trailer=\"help:Junio\" --trailer=\"help:Couder\" "
"<msg.txt\n"
"subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:442
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Helped-by: Junio C Hamano <gitster@pobox.com>\n"
"Helped-by: Christian Couder <christian.couder@gmail.com>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:447
msgid ""
"Configure a 'ref' trailer with a cmd use a script `glog-grep` to grep last "
"relevant commit from git log in the git repository and show how it works:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:454
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ cat ~/bin/glog-grep\n"
"#!/bin/sh\n"
"test -n \"$1\" && git log --grep \"$1\" --pretty=reference -1 || true\n"
"$ cat msg.txt\n"
"subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:461
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"body text\n"
"$ git config trailer.ref.key \"Reference-to: \"\n"
"$ git config trailer.ref.ifExists \"replace\"\n"
"$ git config trailer.ref.cmd \"~/bin/glog-grep\"\n"
"$ git interpret-trailers --trailer=\"ref:Add copyright notices.\" <msg.txt\n"
"subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:465
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reference-to: 8bc9a0c769 (Add copyright notices., 2005-04-07)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:469
msgid ""
"Configure a 'see' trailer with a command to show the subject of a commit "
"that is related, and show how it works:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:486
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"see: HEAD~2\n"
"$ cat ~/bin/glog-ref\n"
"#!/bin/sh\n"
"git log -1 --oneline --format=\"%h (%s)\" --abbrev-commit --abbrev=14\n"
"$ git config trailer.see.key \"See-also: \"\n"
"$ git config trailer.see.ifExists \"replace\"\n"
"$ git config trailer.see.ifMissing \"doNothing\"\n"
"$ git config trailer.see.cmd \"glog-ref\"\n"
"$ git interpret-trailers --trailer=see <msg.txt\n"
"subject\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:490
#, no-wrap
msgid "See-also: fe3187489d69c4 (subject of related commit)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:497
msgid ""
"Configure a commit template with some trailers with empty values (using sed "
"to show and keep the trailing spaces at the end of the trailers), then "
"configure a commit-msg hook that uses 'git interpret-trailers' to remove "
"trailers with empty values and to add a 'git-version' trailer:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:501
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ cat temp.txt\n"
"***subject***\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:503
#, no-wrap
msgid "***message***\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-interpret-trailers.txt:515
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fixes: Z\n"
"Cc: Z\n"
"Reviewed-by: Z\n"
"Signed-off-by: Z\n"
"$ sed -e 's/ Z$/ /' temp.txt > commit_template.txt\n"
"$ git config commit.template commit_template.txt\n"
"$ cat .git/hooks/commit-msg\n"
"#!/bin/sh\n"
"git interpret-trailers --trim-empty --trailer \"git-version: \\$(git "
"describe)\" \"\\$1\" > \"\\$1.new\"\n"
"mv \"\\$1.new\" \"\\$1\"\n"
"$ chmod +x .git/hooks/commit-msg\n"
msgstr ""

